<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.meme.normalizes ~ the normalize law, sealed to disk

`lares meme normalize <file.mem…>` runs the frame law over each named carrier, re-frames what drifted and re-stamps its block check over the body it follows, writing the result in place. `--grammar` also applies the grammar-authority clauses (authored bytes, such as a call site's `:` against `=`); without it those clauses stand proposed and move no byte. It refuses a glob sweep and takes no `--format`; it names every dirty carrier nobody named and carries on, so one hand never seals another hand's half-finished work unseen. Local, no daemon.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ normalize · grammar

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`normalize` params=`files/draft.mem ~ re-frame and re-stamp one carrier`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`grammar` params=`files/draft.mem grammar/true ~ apply the grammar clauses too`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

